{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1523474-narkissos-gentry","id":1523474,"title":"Narkissos (Gentry)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-10-02T14:50:00-07:00","id":1523474,"title":"Narkissos (Gentry)","content":"<i>I've been picking away at a project that's tentatively <b>Night Horrors: Kindly Ones </b>for a little while in the back of my head. Some of the rough drafts are up on my Patreon and I shared another today, so I thought I'd kick one over on the the forums too. Enjoy! This one was written with the Seven Wonders Dark Era in mind, but works perfectly find in the modern day too. </i><br /> <br /> Desperate, stupid Narkissos. That isn't an insult, it's Narkissos' mantra. He doesn't need to be smart, his Titles can be smart for him. All he must do is be deeply, profoundly gorgeous and have a mirror with which he could gaze in his reflection. Or at least, that is how things are supposed to go, which misses the rather salient fact that Narkissos doesn't have any Titles right now. Grandmother, Grandmother and the Ponifex Curciatus tore them away from him, taking with them whatever wit and cunning he possessed.<br /> <br /> Now, Narkissos is desperate and defenceless. He is beautiful and knows how to use that beauty to his own advantage, but he is prone to acting rashly and fixating upon himself when he would be better served by being proactive. While no True Fae is easy to take down, Narkissos makes a tempting target for changelings wishing to rid the world of the Others. Narkissos is well aware of this and intends to use one simple fact as an aegis to hold them back.<br /> <br /> He has never been a Keeper.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s no altruism in Narkissos\u2019 (lack of) actions. For one, he is far too egocentric to believe that any mortal could be more interesting than his own face. It's not like he doesn\u2019t interfere with mortals either, he is well known as a dream-thief and bauble-forger. He knows, however, just how much the Lost hate his peers and is willing to help them if it means regaining a Title.<br /> <br /> Narkissos appears to be a young man in his late teens or early twenties. He is as beautiful as humanly possible, which is a point of wounded pride for him, as he was once superhumanly gorgeous. His Regalia is a crown of liquid mirrors, woven together with flowering narcissuses. This crown appears mundane through Narkissos' Mask, but the mirrored surfaces seem to ripple as if they are water. In his Mein, halos of water and flowers surround Narkissos, giving him an air of unearthly grace.<br /> <br /> <b>Three Rumours</b><br /> <br /> <i>\u201cNarkissos declared his estate a safe haven for changelings in Arcadia! He gathers the freeholds to his banner so we can break the Keepers\u2019 hold on our people once and for all!\u201d</i><br /> <br /> This rumour has a grain of truth in it, but it is only the barest hint. Narkissos\u2019 realm is relatively safe for changelings, but that is only because he is desperate for allies. He has no plans to put himself at risk for (as he sees it) lesser creatures. More often than not, this rumour starts with Huntsmen or Privateers who set up ambushes a safe distance away from the desperate Fae\u2019s holdings.<br /> <br /> <i>\u201cThe Kindly Ones are liars and Narkissos is no different. He will tell you he isn\u2019t a Keeper and he might now be one now \u2014 but that\u2019s only because he lost the Title. Don\u2019t fall for his pretty lies.\u201d</i><br /> <br /> While this is a common sentiment, Narkissos is being truthful when he says he isn\u2019t a Keeper. He has no qualms about interfering with mortals\u2019 lives, however, he just doesn\u2019t steal and twist them to his own will. It is entirely possible for changelings to find lost heirlooms, missing childhood toys, or even stolen dreams while wandering his domain.<br /> <br /> <i>\u201cNarkissos has his very own cult. He recruits mortals, fae-touched, changelings, and even stranger beings to lead weird (or Wyrd) rites dedicated to his beauty.\u201d</i><br /> <br /> This is wholly true. Ever the self-aggrandizer, Narkissos has an entire cult of loyalists and mortals who worship him as a god. Artists, hedonists, and occultists find a safe space within their ranks; occasionally, non-fae supernal beings even join, seeking power from the faerie god.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><b>Narkissos</b></b></span><br /> <b>Associated Seeming: </b>Fairest<br /> <b>Needle:</b> Bon Vivant<br /> <b>Thread: </b>Joy<br /> <b>Aspirations: </b>Regaina Title, Steal a dream, Create a monument to himself<br /> <b>Attributes:</b> Intelligence 1, Wits 2, Resolve 1; Strength 4, Dexterity 3, Stamina 3; Presence 5, Manipulation 5, Composure 1<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Occult 3, Politics 3; Athletics 5; Animal Ken 2, Expression 4, Persuasion 5, Socialize 3<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Defensive Dreamscaping, Dreamweaver, Inspiring, Striking Looks 2<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 2<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> +4<br /> <b>Defence:</b> 2 (4 in dreams)<br /> <b>Armor:</b> 0<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 12<br /> <b>Health:</b> 8<br /> <b>Wyrd:</b> 5<br /> <b>Glamour/per Turn:</b> 15/5<br /> <b>Banes:</b> Iron, Oath to acknowledge no-one's beauty but his own<br /> <b>Regalia:</b> Crown<br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-02T17:08:28-07:00","id":1523480,"title":"","content":"\u201cKindly Ones\u201d is a good name for a Night Horrors title, and Narkissos is a nice background character <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc